        <section id="what-is-the-purpose-of-written-communications-used-in-cyber-security."  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>What is the purpose of written communications used in cyber security.</h2>
              <p>The field of cyber security has changed a lot over the last 25 years and the skill of communication has become more important and crucial to the development of cyber security initiatives. Cyber security professionals need to be able to communicate highly technical details to others who may not always have the technical knowledge. They will be asked to create a variety of written reports which will have to put forward technical details to others within a company without the same technical background in an informative but clear way that get that information across.</p>
<p>Let's look at some of the written reports that are used in cyber security.</p>

              
              
<div class="gallery-container">
  <div role="group" class="gallery no-js">
    <ul>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Vulnerability reports
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>A vulnerability report should be a succinct document which prioritises the critical issues in a list and details the ease of remediation because it’s often impractical to fix every vulnerability. A business needs to know which issues can be fixed and which will have the most impact given that resources may be restricted. Because these are usually generated by vulnerability software and the volume of vulnerabilities will be high, accuracy is not as important.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u6_s3_p1_slide1.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Penetration Testing reports
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Penetration tests (Pen Tests) should be similar to vulnerability reports but because they are created by humans in a limited time period there will often be fewer to report and higher in criticality. They should go into more detail and be able to be utilised by a non-cyber security audience than vulnerability. The most important part of a pen test report are;</p>
<ul>
<li>the steps to fix the problem</li>
<li>executive summary as a high level overview of the general security of the system for the executive team</li>
<li>how the results were found</li>
</ul>
<p>Because these are vulnerabilities found by software then validated by humans, accuracy is much more important in these documents than in a normal vulnerability reports.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u6_s3_p1_slide2.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Incident reports
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>An incident report is often given to external customers if they have been affected, and in some cases a regulatory body such as the ICO and therefore needs to be an accurate professional document. It should contain a general overview of what has happened in non-technical language for everyone to understand.</p>
<p>It should also include a timeline for legal purposes to show step by step what has happened. The most important part is a section detailing what lessons have been learned from the incident and what will be done to ensure that it doesn’t happen again.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u6_s3_p1_slide3.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Internal policy documents
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Internal policy documents dictate what an employee can and cannot do. Because it’s audience is wide and non-technical it is important that the language is understandable by all. The use of language is extremely important, making sure that the correct tenses and words are used at all times as well as the correct tone of voice.
These policies form the rules an employee has to abide by and they are often used in disciplinary hearings, they therefore need to be accurate and clear in what they require of all employees.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cs/cs_u6_s3_p1_slide4.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
